.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_REQ_GET_ATTR 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_REQ_get_attr_count ,
.Nm X509_REQ_get_attr_by_NID ,
.Nm X509_REQ_get_attr_by_OBJ ,
.Nm X509_REQ_get_attr ,
.Nm X509_REQ_delete_attr ,
.Nm X509_REQ_add1_attr ,
.Nm X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_OBJ ,
.Nm X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_NID ,
.Nm X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_txt
.NdX509_ATTRIBUTE No support for signed certificate requests
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_get_attr_count
.Fa "const X509_REQ *req"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_get_attr_by_NID
.Fa "const X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "int nid"
.Fa "int lastpos"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_get_attr_by_OBJ
.Fa "const X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "const ASN1_OBJECT *obj"
.Fa "int lastpos"
.Fc
.Ft X509_ATTRIBUTE *
.Fo X509_REQ_get_attr
.Fa "const X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "int loc"
.Fc
.Ft X509_ATTRIBUTE *
.Fo X509_REQ_delete_attr
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "int loc"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_add1_attr
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "X509_ATTRIBUTE *attr"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_OBJ
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "const ASN1_OBJECT *obj"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "const unsigned char *bytes"
.Fa "int len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_NID
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "int nid"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "const unsigned char *bytes"
.Fa "int len"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_txt
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "const char *attrname"
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "const unsigned char *bytes"
.Fa "int len"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_by_OBJ
finds the location of the first matching object
.Fa obj
in the
.Fa req
attribute list.
The search starts at the position after
.Fa lastpos .
If the returned value is positive then it can be used on the next call
to
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_by_OBJ
as the value of
.Fa lastpos
in order to iterate through the remaining attributes.
.Fa lastpos
can be set to any negative value on the first call, in order to start
searching from the start of the attribute list.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_by_NID
is similar to
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_by_OBJ
except that it passes the numerical identifier (NID)
.Fa nid
associated with the object.
See <openssl/obj_mac.h> for a list of NID_*.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr
returns the
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
object at index
.Fa loc
in the
.Fa req
attribute list.
.Fa loc
should be in the range from 0 to
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_count
- 1.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_delete_attr
removes the
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
object at index
.Fa loc
in the
.Fa req
objects list of attributes.
An error occurs if
.Fa req
is NULL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr
pushes a copy of the passed in
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
.Em Ns attr>
to the
.Fa req
object's attribute list.
An error will occur if either the attribute list is NULL or the
attribute already exists.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_OBJ
creates a new
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
using
.Xr X509_ATTRIBUTE_set1_object 3
and
.Xr X509_ATTRIBUTE_set1_data 3
to assign a new
.Fa obj
with type
.Fa type
and data
.Fa bytes
of length
.Fa len
and then pushes it to the
.Fa req
object's attribute list.
.Fa req
must be non NULL or an error will occur.
If
.Fa obj
already exists in the attribute list then an error occurs.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_NID
is similar to
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_OBJ
except that it passes the numerical identifier (NID)
.Fa nid
associated with the object.
See <openssl/obj_mac.h> for a list of NID_*.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_txt
is similar to
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_OBJ
except that it passes a name
.Fa attrname
associated with the object.
See <openssl/obj_mac.h> for a list of SN_* names.
.Pp
Refer to
.Xr X509_ATTRIBUTE 3
for information related to attributes.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_count
returns the number of attributes in the
.Fa req
object attribute list or -1 if the attribute list is NULL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_by_OBJ
returns -1 if either the
.Fa req
object's attribute list is empty OR
.Fa obj
is not found, otherwise it returns the location of the
.Fa obj
in the attribute list.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_by_NID
is similar to
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr_by_OBJ ,
except that it returns -2 if the
.Fa nid
is not known by OpenSSL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_get_attr
returns either an
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_delete_attr
returns either the removed
.Vt X509_ATTRIBUTE
or NULL if there is a error.
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr ,
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_OBJ ,
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_NID
and
.Fn X509_REQ_add1_attr_by_txt
return 1 on success or 0 on error.
.Sh NOTES
Any functions that modify the attributes (add or delete) internally set
a flag to indicate the ASN.1 encoding has been modified.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr X509_ATTRIBUTE 3
